    {
     "id": "ba814787-17ee-4673-81ad-889abfe82625",
     "prompt": "Make $x$ the subject of $x(a+3)=b(x-2)$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$x=\\frac{2b}{a+3-b}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$x=\\frac{-2b}{a+3+b}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$x=\\frac{-2b}{a+3-b}$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$x=\\frac{b-2}{a+3-b}$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Expand to get $ax+3x=bx-2b$. Collecting the terms containing $x$ gives $x(a+3-b)=-2b$, so $x=\\frac{-2b}{a+3-b}$."
