    {
     "id": "2f368b4b-e133-4d9b-9325-af3548f464a8",
     "prompt": "Make $p$ the subject of $q^2=p^2+6s$, with no information restricting the sign of $p$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$p=q^2-6s$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$p=\\sqrt{q^2+6s}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$p=\\sqrt{q^2-6s}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$p=\\pm\\sqrt{q^2-6s}$",
       "correct": true
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "First isolate the squared term: $p^2=q^2-6s$. Taking the square root gives both possible signs, so $p=\\pm\\sqrt{q^2-6s}$."
